s or something  that roughly translates into  i've played this level a bunch of times  and i didn't  magically complete it  so it must take luck  and  i don't know how many times you'd have  to play this one over and over in order  to get lucky to finish it but i would  think it would be in the hundreds  all right so here we are this is where  everything  gets real important  all right so this is where things where  you really have to um  plan things out and it's frustrating  because it's a really small space here  so  we have 21 moves which is not bad  if you have less than that it's going to  be tough most of the time  but what i figured out that helped me a  lot  to finally finish it and hopefully  finish it here again  is um  there's there's a color bomb right here  and there's a coloring candy right here  this stuff on the side has a lot of  layers and there's bears there too but  the hardest pairs to get are always in  this last row  and since this board is pretty good for  cascades  rather than trying to go left and right  it's much better to go straight down  and things will start to open up a lot  faster  if you go in a straight line so  in situations like this yeah we want to  make the um  we can fire out the stripes which is  going to go where we want but we'd want  to make the um  wrap candy first because it'll drop down  and  we got another wrap so i think here  what we'll want to do is instead of  firing that off at all we'll use  we'll use the double wrap because it's  going to end up right around here  and give us a nice five by five  explosion  and it'll shoot off this anyway so  so at this point we've um  we've used up five of our moves  but look how much of the sides and  things that we got cleared out without  even really focusing on those  so we'll scan the board  we do want to look  for spots where we might be able to make  color bombs or coloring candies  but we know that we have them right here  so  since i don't see anything  really fantasti